* 14 Sep 26 Windows port - RELEASE_1.1 5 stage 2a: $INCLUDE is found as either
*           $INCLUDE or $include.
* 19 Aug 26 Windows port - the default source file is bp, not BP.  5.12 (b).
* 17 Oct 26 dm  S.64 part 2 (the edit gates): GENERATE writes into two files the user names, the dictionary (the $INCLUDE control
*               record it makes when there is none) and the target file of that record (bp by default; the include records), and
*               it is $internal, so the kernel's own test lets both through.  Each now asks edit_guard, the dictionary before the
*               questions about the record are put, the target file once, before an include record is opened.
* 06 Oct 26 dm  PAL-1 stage 2a (parity audit; the Windows port's RELEASE_1.1 5): a
*               dictionary read folds case, as typed then lower then upper.
* 13 Sep 26 dm  The default source file is bp, not BP (plan M3 D3; the port's
*               1943704).
* 12 Sep 26 dm  Name lookups fold as typed, then lower, then upper (plan M1).
* 19 Jan 04  0.6.1 SD launch. Earlier history details suppressed.
